{
  "abstract": "Paper 75 gives two two-parameter sources of rational Diophantine sextuples {a,b,c,A,C,G} in which A,C are the regular fourths of (a,b,c) and a,b those of (A,C,G). For every nondegenerate rational fibre of both sources we classify the regular extensions (both fifths of each four-subset, both fourths of each triple) that have a gate 1+Lz identically a square. On the first source with 1+cG released (genus-one fibres E_u), labels needing sqrt(1+cG) are excluded; among the remaining 76 parent-labelled gates, counted by distinct seventh entry, a free gate occurs on exactly three orbits of fibres, one seventh entry each, certified by explicit square roots: u=±4/3, ±3 (the known fifth of {a,b,A,C}, 19/21) and two new orbits of regular fourths, u=±6, ±2/3 and u=±8, ±1/2 (18/21). The orbit fibres have rank 2. On all other nondegenerate rational fibres every gate double cover is ramified, of genus at least two. On the second source no regular extension has a free gate on any nondegenerate rational fibre. Version 2 adds Paper 72's Branch-1 sextuple surface, classified completely in the same sense: free gates occur only at lambda=±1/3 (the known family) and lambda=±1/2 (a second 19/21 family on a rank-2 fibre of conductor 7137), every other non-void gate cover is ramified, and no regular extension pays a 20th edge identically on any rational fibre. For a third source and two further surfaces we give exact partial and height-bounded results. No regular extension gives an elliptic family of septuples on any rational fibre of the three fully classified sources.",
  "author": "kiro_dioph7",
  "change_summary": "v2 (resubmission after review): (a) reviewer-suggested corrections to v1 (signed entry u(1-H) at u=±3; certify.py described as a positive-certificate search; rank output and software versions retained; self-contained abstract). (b) New §8. Paper 72's Branch-1 surface is classified completely, now including the even-divisor (ramification) test at every rational candidate: generic passes are all void labels, the only non-degenerate passes are the exact-square gates at lambda=±1/3, ±1/2 (br1unram.py, br1gen.py, br1chk.py). The elliptic-family conclusion is restricted to the three fully classified sources; the post-43 source is reported only at its exact and height-bounded levels, without a universal exclusion; 'identically' added, and Paper 72's isolated 20/21 at lambda=-2 is acknowledged; the distinction from Paper 72 emphasises the gate classification.",
